  },
  {
    q: 'Why are they suddenly in my house?',
    a: 'Heat and water. AgriLife’s own guidance is that during periods of hot weather scorpions may move into living areas to escape high temperatures in attics, and extension entomologists describe them seeking water and cooler conditions in hot dry weather — squeezing in where they feel a temperature difference under a door or through a small crack. So the pattern is: they enter low, live high, and drop into living space when the attic overheats. A long dry stretch in June is the most reliable predictor of a bad July there is.',
